## Deploy in 6 steps

You don't need a terminal. Everything below happens in a browser.

### 1 · Push this code to GitHub

You have two options. **A** is easier if you're new to Git.

**A. GitHub web upload**
1. Go to **https://github.com/new** → name it `lifeos` → **Private** → **Create repository**.
2. On the empty repo page, click **uploading an existing file**.
3. Drag every file and folder from this project (except `node_modules/` if it exists — it shouldn't) into the upload area.
4. Commit message: `initial scaffold` → **Commit changes**.

**B. StackBlitz (recommended once set up — gives you live preview)**
1. Go to **https://stackblitz.com** → sign in with GitHub.
2. **New project → SvelteKit** (or import this zip via the UI).
3. Drag-drop all files in. StackBlitz will install dependencies automatically.
4. Click the **Connect Repository** button → choose `lifeos`. From now on, "Commit" pushes to GitHub.

### 2 · Connect Netlify

1. Go to **https://app.netlify.com** → **Add new site → Import an existing project → GitHub**.
2. Pick the `lifeos` repo.
3. Build settings should auto-fill (build command `npm run build`, publish directory `build`). If not, set them.
4. **Do not deploy yet** — click "Add environment variables" first, or go to **Site settings → Environment variables** after the first failed deploy.

### 3 · Set environment variables in Netlify

Add these (Site settings → Environment variables → Add variable). Use the values from your Supabase, Whoop, and Anthropic accounts (the **rotated** ones).

| Name | Value |
|---|---|
| `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` | `https://quganjzukmadvblxhbjx.supabase.co` |
| `PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | _your rotated anon key_ |
| `PUBLIC_APP_URL` | _your Netlify URL, e.g. `https://lifeos-xyz.netlify.app`_ |
| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | _your rotated Anthropic key_ |
| `WHOOP_CLIENT_ID` | `c5b5feda-1bcf-4e2e-b3d5-bc30cb2340e3` |
| `WHOOP_CLIENT_SECRET` | _your rotated Whoop secret_ |

> The first three are needed for v0.1 to work. The last three are needed in upcoming stages.

After adding variables, click **Deploys → Trigger deploy → Deploy site**.

### 4 · Configure Supabase to allow your Netlify URL

1. In Supabase → **Authentication → URL Configuration**.
2. **Site URL**: your Netlify URL (e.g. `https://lifeos-xyz.netlify.app`).
3. **Redirect URLs**: add both your Netlify URL and `http://localhost:5173` (so you can run it locally later).
4. Save.

### 5 · Try it

1. Visit your Netlify URL.
2. Click **Get started**, create an account.
3. Confirm via the email Supabase sends.
4. Sign in → log a workout. You should see it appear on the dashboard.

### 6 · Add the live URL to Whoop

1. **https://developer.whoop.com** → your app → **Redirect URLs** → add `https://YOUR-NETLIFY-URL/auth/whoop/callback`.
2. We'll wire this up in the next stage.

